# Challenges

Some scene categories such as glacier and mountain contained visually similar images, which sometimes caused classification confusion.

Training time was also relatively long because transfer learning models require more computational resources.

Another challenge was balancing model complexity and overfitting prevention.

---

# Conclusion

The final deep learning model successfully classified natural scene images into six categories using transfer learning.

Using MobileNetV2 with data augmentation and dropout significantly improved performance compared to the baseline CNN model.

The project demonstrated the effectiveness of transfer learning for image classification tasks and provided practical experience with preprocessing, training, evaluation, and deep learning experimentation.

